    "['no auto-summary', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-options autonomous-system 100 no-validate', 'parent_command': ['set protocols bgp local-as [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set protocols bgp local-as [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset routing-options autonomous-system 100 no-validate\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact equivalent of Cisco's `no auto-summary` in BGP doesn't exist in Juniper because Juniper routers don't perform automatic network summarization by default (they behave as if `no auto-summary` is always enabled). However, the closest related command in Juniper is the one shown above, which disables AS path validation for the local AS (100 in this case), though this isn't a direct translation. \\n\\nA more accurate approach would be to simply omit any auto-summary command in Juniper, as this behavior is default. If you specifically need to ensure classful network summarization is disabled (the effect of `no auto-summary` in Cisco), no explicit command is needed in Juniper as this isn't supported.\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-options autonomous-system 100 no-validate'}]]": 1,
